				972,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Decompose Workspace RPC handlers into file-per-struct modules\n\nDecompose the `Source/RPC/CocoonService/Workspace` module to align with the project-wide PascalCase file-per-struct convention. Extract the handler logic for `ApplyEdit`, `OpenDocument`, `SaveAll`, `UpdateConfiguration`, and `UpdateWorkspaceFolders` into dedicated submodules.\n\nEach handler is exposed as a public async function `Fn` within its own file, invoked via fully qualified paths in the parent `mod.rs`. The implementations bridge the gRPC `Vine` protocol to the frontend: `ApplyEdit`, `OpenDocument`, `SaveAll`, and `UpdateConfiguration` emit specific Tauri events to the `Sky` UI layer, while `UpdateWorkspaceFolders` performs direct mutation of the `ApplicationState.Workspace` DTOs and triggers the standard notification mechanism. This preserves all existing logic for text editing ranges, untitled file handling, and folder index stability, ensuring consistent symbol resolution for Tauri's `generate_handler!` macro.",
			"SHA": "3ad7df3dc9d9447ced7b2baf5725e63fb4752381"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T05:37:15Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				966,
				16
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Decompose CocoonService RPC handlers into file-per-struct modules\n\nDecompose the monolithic `Source/RPC/CocoonService` modules to align with the project-wide PascalCase file-per-struct convention. Extract the handler logic for every gRPC entry point across Auth, Command, Debug, Extension, FileSystem, Initialization, Output, Provider, SCM, Secret, Task, Terminal, TreeView, Window, and Workspace into dedicated submodules (e.g., `Command/RegisterCommand.rs`, `FileSystem/ReadFile.rs`, `Window/ShowTextDocument.rs`).\n\nEach handler is now exposed as a function within its own module and invoked via the fully qualified path `Module::Function::Fn` in the main `mod.rs` implementation. This mirrors the architectural pattern established in recent `Workspace`, `Echo`, and `Telemetry` refactors. The changes preserve all existing logic, including the TreeView emission batching, SCM state tracking, and webview panel lifecycle management, while ensuring correct symbol resolution for Tauri's `generate_handler!` macro and gRPC wire protocol generation.",
			"SHA": "ef96dfe524b73c7c862a7a1c74bf8088065d5b35"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T05:36:33Z",
